course: dictionary
lesson: 5237
title: Jewellery: a word for things we wear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Jewellery is a word for decorations people wear, such as rings, necklaces, bracelets, earrings and brooches. Many pieces are made of metal, gems or beads.
explain: Jewellery is uncountable, so we do not add an s. You say «gold jewellery» or «a piece of jewellery», not «two jewelleries». To count it, use the words piece of.
explain: Read the sentence for clues: «Pure gold is so soft that it scratches easily, so most gold jewellery is gold mixed with other metals.» Gold jewellery is jewellery made of gold, and the sentence tells you why gold is often mixed with other metals.
fact: Jewellery means decorations people wear, such as rings, necklaces, bracelets, earrings and brooches.
fact: Jewellery is often made of metal, gems or beads.
fact: Jewellery is an uncountable noun: say «some jewellery» or «a piece of jewellery», never «jewelleries».
fact: People wear jewellery for decoration, for their culture, and at special events.
fact: In PE lessons, jewellery is often not allowed because it can catch and cause injuries.
exercise: What is jewellery? | Large pieces of furniture | *Decorations people wear, such as rings and necklaces | Tools used for gardening | Clothes for swimming in the sea
exercise: Jewellery is uncountable. Which phrase is correct? | many jewelleries | *a piece of jewellery | three jewelleries | two jewelleries
exercise: «Pure gold is so soft that it scratches easily, so most gold jewellery is gold mixed with other metals.» Why is gold often mixed with other metals? | *Pure gold is soft and scratches easily | Gold is always mixed with glass | Pure gold is too hard to wear | Gold cannot be shiny
test: Which of these is a piece of jewellery? | A blanket | A bucket | A broom | *A brooch
test: «Ancient jewellery found in graves tells us about past people.» What does this sentence tell us? | Past people never wore any decorations | Graves are full of jewellery boxes | *Past people wore decorations, and jewellery from graves helps us learn about them | Ancient jewellery is always made of plastic
exam: Which sentence uses jewellery correctly? | I bought two jewelleries at the market. | *I bought a lovely piece of jewellery at the market. | I bought many jewellerys at the market. | I bought three jewelleries at the market.
